# Rust / Cargo
# The workspace lives at the repository root (T1), so cargo's output is ./target
# — 24 GB of it on a working tree. `rust/target/` used to be listed alongside
# this for the pre-T1 `rust/` crate; that path has not existed since the crate
# was renamed to `core/`, so T14 dropped the entry.
target/

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*.iml

# Flatpak (T4/D26b: verify.sh pins --state-dir and the build dir inside
# .flatpak-builder/, which flatpak-builder self-ignores via its own
# .gitignore; `repo/` is named so a future --repo=repo regression fails
# loudly here instead of landing untracked.)
.flatpak/
.flatpak-builder/
repo/
# test_packaging.py imports the generator via importlib, which writes
# flatpak/__pycache__/ on every run — build bytecode, never committed.
__pycache__/

# Environment and secrets
.env
.aider*

# Misc
*.log

# RPM build artifacts
# build-rpm.sh copies the built RPM into the repository root, and the spec's
# Source0 is a `%{name}-%{version}.tar.gz` source tarball, so both need to be
# ignored: an 18 MB `gosh-distrobox-manager-1.0.0-linux-x64.tar.gz` was
# committed once and only deleted in T14. This guard is what stops the next
# `git add -A` from putting it (or its successor) back.
*.rpm
*.src.rpm
rpmbuild/
gosh-distrobox-manager-*.tar.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Retired in T14 with the Flutter tree. Kept here as a record of what used to
# be ignored and why it no longer is, rather than silently vanishing:
#
#   .dart_tool/ .packages .metadata pubspec.lock
#   .flutter-plugins .flutter-plugins-dependencies
#       Dart/Flutter tooling state. No Dart toolchain is involved any more.
#   flutter_output.txt*
#       Scratch output from the old Flutter launcher shim.
#   build/
#       Flutter's output directory. Nothing in this workspace writes it now:
#       cargo uses target/, flatpak-builder uses .flatpak-builder/, and the
#       meson `_build/` went with the meson build. If something does create it,
#       it should land untracked and visible rather than be silently ignored.
#   rust/target/, _build/
#       Pre-T1 crate path and the meson build dir; neither directory exists.
#   test_spawn, plans/
#       Flutter-era scratch names. `.flatpak-builder`-style self-ignoring tools
#       cover their own output; nothing produces these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
